<section class="panel" aria-label="Grade3 original U06 L06 metric weight estimation first-party">
<h2>Estimate and Measure Weight</h2>
<p>Source warm-up Produce Stand is open: describe observations about weights of produce, how store workers could use weighing and appropriate questions. Original third-party photographs are not reproduced.</p>
<h3>Activity1: all five original physical reference weights</h3><table class="source-chart"><thead><tr><th>Source prepared weight</th><th>Student's approximate same-weight example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>1 gram</th><td>______________________ (teacher checks)</td></tr><tr><th>10 grams</th><td>______________________ (teacher checks)</td></tr><tr><th>100 grams</th><td>______________________ (teacher checks)</td></tr><tr><th>1 kilogram</th><td>______________________ (teacher checks)</td></tr><tr><th>2 kilograms</th><td>______________________ (teacher checks)</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Teacher prepares one set of reference weights, then groups rotate (five groups, two minutes each). An ordinary paperclip is about1g; basket of apples about1kg in the original lesson. Use actual tactile comparison rather than pretending classroom objects have one fixed weight.</p>
<h3>Four original classroom sorting categories</h3><table class="source-chart"><thead><tr><th>Original weight range</th><th>Real object student finds</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>less than 1 gram</th><td>__________________</td></tr><tr><th>between 1 gram and 100 grams</th><td>__________________</td></tr><tr><th>between 100 grams and 1 kilogram</th><td>__________________</td></tr><tr><th>more than 1 kilogram</th><td>__________________</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h3>Activity2: four pets and four plausible original matching cards</h3><table class="source-chart"><thead><tr><th>Original pet</th><th>One reasonable source weight card</th><th>Why reasonable?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>guinea pig</th><td>1 kilogram</td><td>Teacher checks explanation</td></tr><tr><th>dog</th><td>20 kilograms</td><td>Teacher checks explanation</td></tr><tr><th>small fish</th><td>3 grams</td><td>Teacher checks explanation</td></tr><tr><th>cat</th><td>3 kilograms</td><td>Teacher checks explanation</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>These are estimated matching possibilities, NOT a measured weight for the pictured animal. A scale or balance can be used if available. Publisher original images, original student PDF and gated Cool-down About a Kilogram are not copied. <a href="https://im.kendallhunt.com/k5/teachers/grade-3/unit-6/lesson-6/lesson.html">Original 2021 teacher lesson</a>.</p></section>